      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Multilateral trade agreements like those managed by the WTO promote global peace and stability by providing a predictable and legal framework for international commerce. These agreements significantly reduce trade barriers such as tariffs and quotas, which allows nations to specialize in their comparative advantages and drive overall economic efficiency for all participants. Furthermore, the dispute settlement mechanisms within these systems resolve conflicts over trade disputes fairly, safeguarding market access and preventing protectionist policies from derailing the modern global economy.",
      "source": "target",
