      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean yeah i get that it's \"contentious\" but if you really look at it, it feels like the globalist approach is just better for everyone in the long run even if it's messy at first. like, isn't it basically a fact that sticking to these international rules is the only way to prevent another massive global depression or trade war? it seems like the sovereignty argument is just an excuse for countries to be selfish and ruin the global system.",
