      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a common argument that upholding international rules is the only effective shield against the catastrophic economic downturns and unrestricted trade wars seen in the 1930s, which I would argue was the primary catalyst for the Great Depression. Supporters often view the perceived erosion of sovereignty as an unfortunate short-term cost for the unparalleled long-term stability and efficiency provided by a unified global market, rejecting the idea that national interests should override collective well-being.",
